# Build output. **/build/ also covers app/build, which holds the APK, the R8 mapping and the
# baseline profiles -- all reproducible from source.
.gradle/
.kotlin/
**/build/
captures/
*.hprof
.gradleletasknamecache

# Packaged artifacts. A Release App Bundle is the Play upload unit and is large, and neither it nor
# a split APK should ever be committed by accident.
*.apk
*.apks
*.aab
*.apkm
*.xapk
*.idsig
*.dex

# Machine-local configuration. local.properties holds sdk.dir, which points at one developer's SDK.
local.properties

# IDE state. .vscode/ is deliberately NOT ignored: its settings.json is shared project
# configuration, unlike the rest of .idea/ which is per-developer and churns constantly.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.fleet/
.tools/

# Release signing material. A published signing key cannot be rotated for an existing Play listing,
# so neither the keystore nor its passwords may ever reach the repository. PKCS12 stores are
# covered by *.p12 and *.pfx as well as *.jks, because keytool's default store type is PKCS12 and
# it is routinely named either way.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.bks
*.pem
*.key
*.pkcs12

# Other secrets and local environment overrides.
.env
.env.*
secrets.properties

# Firebase Android config. It carries the project's API key and OAuth client ids, it is per-machine
# (the OAuth client is bound to a signing-certificate SHA-1), and it is re-downloadable from the
# Firebase console, so it never belongs in the repository.
google-services.json

# Firebase and Google Cloud CLI output. The debug logs can contain project identifiers, auth
# tokens and emulator traffic, so they are never useful in a repository.
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
database-debug.log
pubsub-debug.log
ui-debug.log
*-debug.log
*.log

# RE research inputs. research/sdk-badging.txt and the screenshots stay tracked, because the findings
# reference them.
research/sdk-resources.txt
research/sdk-manifest.txt
research/base-artifact.json
research/emulator.log
research/*-ui.xml

# The extracted Google Docs APK bundle used for the RE research. `*.apk` above already excludes the
# APKs themselves, but the directory also holds Google's icon.png and their META-INF/APKMIRRO
# signing signature blocks. Those are Google's packaged assets and their signature material, they
# are analysis inputs rather than project source, and README.md states that no packaged assets were
# copied into the app. Nothing here belongs in the repository. The evidence summary that research
# actually depends on stays in research/, and the full archive stays local as before.
com.google.android.apps.docs.editors.docs/

# Node tooling, if site/ ever gains a build step.
node_modules/
.npm/

# Editor and operating system noise. *.orig and *.rej are conflict leftovers from a bad merge or a
# failed patch, which is exactly the kind of file that gets committed by accident and then lives in
# history forever.
*~
*.swp
*.swo
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# Firestore emulator local state, created by firebase emulators:exec.
.firebase/
